---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { MenubarEditor, MenubarPlayground } from "../../components/MenubarDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Menubar"
  description="A row of app menus with items, shortcuts, checkboxes, radio groups, and submenus."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Menubar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A row of menus, like the File and View menus of a desktop app. Use it for an
    editor or tool that has many commands. For one set of actions, use a
    Dropdown Menu.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="menubar-demo"><MenubarPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Menubar usage"
      code={`import {
  Menubar,
  MenubarCheckboxItem,
  MenubarContent,
  MenubarItem,
  MenubarMenu,
  MenubarRadioGroup,
  MenubarRadioItem,
  MenubarSeparator,
  MenubarShortcut,
  MenubarSub,
  MenubarSubContent,
  MenubarSubTrigger,
  MenubarTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/menubar";

<Menubar aria-label="Application menu">
  <MenubarMenu>
    <MenubarTrigger>File</MenubarTrigger>
    <MenubarContent>
      <MenubarItem onClick={newDraft}>
        New draft<MenubarShortcut>⌘ N</MenubarShortcut>
      </MenubarItem>
      <MenubarItem disabled>Print</MenubarItem>
      <MenubarSeparator />
      <MenubarItem variant="destructive" onClick={discard}>Discard draft</MenubarItem>
    </MenubarContent>
  </MenubarMenu>
  <MenubarMenu>
    <MenubarTrigger>View</MenubarTrigger>
    <MenubarContent>
      <MenubarCheckboxItem checked={sidebar} onCheckedChange={setSidebar}>
        Show sidebar
      </MenubarCheckboxItem>
      <MenubarRadioGroup value={density} onValueChange={setDensity}>
        <MenubarRadioItem value="compact">Compact</MenubarRadioItem>
        <MenubarRadioItem value="comfortable">Comfortable</MenubarRadioItem>
      </MenubarRadioGroup>
      <MenubarSub>
        <MenubarSubTrigger>More</MenubarSubTrigger>
        <MenubarSubContent>
          <MenubarItem onClick={zoomIn}>Zoom in</MenubarItem>
        </MenubarSubContent>
      </MenubarSub>
    </MenubarContent>
  </MenubarMenu>
</Menubar>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants and states</h2>
    <p>
      <code>MenubarItem variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> or <code
        >"destructive"</code
      >; destructive items use the danger color and a tinted highlight. <code
        >disabled</code
      > items stay readable at half opacity and can still be reached with arrow keys.
      Checkbox and radio items show a check at the start, so rows without a check
      use <code>inset</code> to line up with them. Long names in a submenu can truncate
      with an ellipsis.
    </p>
    <MenubarEditor client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="menubar-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Menubar</code> wraps the Base UI menubar and takes <code>modal</code
      >, <code>disabled</code>, <code>orientation</code>, and <code
        >loopFocus</code
      >. Give it an <code>aria-label</code>. <code>MenubarMenu</code>, <code
        >MenubarTrigger</code
      >, <code>MenubarPortal</code>, <code>MenubarGroup</code>, <code
        >MenubarSub</code
      >, <code>MenubarRadioGroup</code>, and <code>MenubarSeparator</code> wrap the
      Base UI menu parts and take their props, including <code>open</code>,
      <code>onOpenChange</code>, and <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>MenubarContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It takes
      <code>side</code> (<code>"bottom"</code>), <code>align</code> (<code
        >"start"</code
      >), <code>sideOffset</code> (8), <code>alignOffset</code> (-4), <code
        >collisionPadding</code
      > (8), <code>container</code>, and every Base UI popup prop. It is at
      least 9rem wide and grows with its items up to 20rem. <code
        >MenubarSubContent</code
      > takes the same props and opens to the right.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>MenubarItem</code> takes <code>variant</code> and <code>inset</code
      >. <code>MenubarLabel</code>, <code>MenubarSubTrigger</code>, and the
      checkbox and radio items take <code>inset</code> too. Put a <code
        >MenubarLabel</code
      > inside a <code>MenubarGroup</code>; the group takes its name from the
      label. <code>MenubarShortcut</code> is a plain <code>span</code> for hint text;
      it does not bind keys. Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The bar has <code>role="menubar"</code> and is one Tab stop. Arrow Left and
      Arrow Right move between triggers, Arrow Down or Enter opens a menu, and while
      a menu is open Arrow Left and Arrow Right move to the next menu. Inside a menu,
      arrow keys move, typing jumps to a matching item, Arrow Right opens a submenu,
      and Escape closes the menu and returns focus to its trigger. A focused trigger
      shows a focus ring.
    </p>
    <p>
      Menus fade and scale in over 120ms. Motion turns off when reduced motion
      is requested. In forced-colors mode the open trigger and highlighted item
      get an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Menubars use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code
        >--sprout-hover</code
      >, <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code
        >--sprout-danger</code
      >, <code>--sprout-danger-subtle</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code
        >--sprout-shadow-control</code
      >, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the panel and control radii.
      They need no brand color, so they look the same with the neutral and
      TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
